  "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point lies *on* the $y$-axis, $1$ unit *below* the origin in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $0,$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-1.$\n\nTherefore, its coordinates are $(0,-1).$",
